//! `forest`: generated by tinymind-rs tools/import_trees/tinymind_import_trees.py
//! from a RandomForestClassifier. Do not edit; regenerate from the model instead.
//!
//! Integer-only and `no_std`. Inputs are `i16` on each feature's grid
//! (`quantize_features` converts a float sample).
//!
//! The output is a vote: each tree names a class, and `forward` counts the votes.
//!
//! Two equivalent forms: `forward`/`predict` walk the node pool with
//! `tinymind::tree` (smaller code), `forward_inline`/`predict_inline` run the
//! same trees compiled to nested `if`s (faster, larger). Both give the same
//! results.

// Not every program uses every item, and the trees are written as trained:
// a split can have two equal leaves, and an `else` holds a nested `if`.
#![allow(dead_code, clippy::if_same_then_else, clippy::collapsible_else_if)]

